# MESH — environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is the template
# and must never hold a real secret.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Everything prefixed VITE_ is read at BUILD time and ends up in the JavaScript
# the browser downloads. That is not a leak for the values below — they are
# public identifiers — but it does mean a real secret must never carry that
# prefix, and that changing one requires a rebuild, not just a restart.


# ─── Front end ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Reown project id, from https://dashboard.reown.com → your project → Project ID.
# Enables WalletConnect, so people can connect a wallet on their phone by
# scanning a QR code. Leave it empty and MESH offers browser wallets only, and
# says so in the picker rather than showing a button that cannot work.
#
# Add every domain you deploy to under the project's Allowed Domains, including
# the Netlify URL, or wallets will show the connection as unverified.
VITE_REOWN_PROJECT_ID=

# Origin of the MESH API, e.g. https://mesh-api.onrender.com
#
# Leave EMPTY when the API and the web app share a host — including local
# development, where the dev server proxies /api and /ws for you.
#
# Set it when they are apart, which is the case on a static host like Netlify:
# the API keeps a SQLite database and a WebSocket open, so it cannot run there
# and lives somewhere that can hold those. No trailing slash.
VITE_API_URL=


# ─── API server ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by `server/index.js` at runtime. These are NOT sent to the browser.

# Where the API listens. Most hosts set PORT themselves — read that first.
# MESH_API_PORT=8787
# MESH_API_HOST=0.0.0.0

# Path to the SQLite file. On a host with a persistent disk, point this at it —
# the default lives inside the checkout and is wiped on every deploy.
# MESH_DB=/data/mesh.db

# Browsers that may call this API cross-origin, comma separated, no trailing
# slash. Required when VITE_API_URL is set; leave empty for same-origin.
# Include the Netlify production URL and any preview domain you actually use.
# MESH_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-site.netlify.app
